# Build context for the Node images (web, console, cms).
#
# Those three used to build with their own directory as the context. They
# cannot any more: this directory is an npm workspace root, the lockfile lives
# here, and `npm ci` inside a single workspace member has no lockfile to read.
# So the context is `engine/` and each Dockerfile builds one member.
#
# Without this file that context is enormous — every .venv under packages/,
# every node_modules, and the .next output of three Next apps.

# Dependency trees and build output — reinstalled inside the image
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.venv
**/dist

# Python tooling that no Node image needs
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Secrets: never in a build context. A COPY . bakes these into a layer that
# survives even if a later step deletes them.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# Local databases, dumps and derived data (docs/data-provenance.md)
**/db/dumps
**/content/harvested
**/*.dump
**/*.jsonl

# Editor and OS noise
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
